WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.920 --> 00:00:12.240 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  [Music]  do  [Music]  so i wrote this piece because recently i  injured my left side and i was stuck  with just using my right hand during  practice  when i was practicing i found it very  difficult to  spot myself when the hand position  changes so for example from here  all the notes are in this position  and i have to jump over to the a  [Music]  so of course i look at the hand  positions as this  and then  this is sort of  divided in two  but when i was trying to bring it up to  tempo i found it very helpful to spot  myself with these off rhythms that i put  in  so this is the beat  [Music]  and a lot of the semitones happen  not on the beat  [Music]  then on the flip side i focused on the  lowest notes of each little section  [Music]  other than that another difficulty i had  was to keep the precision in the tips of  my fingers while having to stretch my  hands so even a stacked fifth like this  my hand has to be stretched to feel  comfortable to play  these three notes  but what happens when the hand is flat  is that the surface area of the finger  that you're using to press the keys  becomes a lot wider a lot bigger  and i find that is is a little  uncomfortable because sometimes if it's  too much you'd bleed over to the next  note and especially at the speed  if the focal point isn't narrower this  key is smaller than  what you're using to play it  so what i did to practice this is to  curl the tips of my fingers at every  single note and play this at a very slow  speed  [Music]  so another thing is endurance for this  piece of course it's very short so it's  not so much of a problem but it is with  the right hand only and it goes at a  very fast tempo  and for the majority of the piece my  hands especially with my size  is stretched out so there's a lot of  tension there's a lot of straining  involved so going back to the first  point i made about anchoring myself to  hear and feel the top ends and the low  ends of each of the different runs  it also helps with relaxation because as  you're making these subtle accents at  those points  it really gives you a chance to drop  into those notes and as you're doing  that you can relax your forearm and your  wrist  so that you're releasing some some  tension there  [Music]  so that's generally it about this piece  and i thank you for watching i'll see  you next time

